text:
You, king of rivers, generous Tagus, who stole motion and warmth from the alabaster body you bathed, graceful, gallant, beautiful;


whether a natural musician among the shells you raised, or offering him the victorious branch from your native valley;


or, your currents freed from ice, giving him a mirror, I ask only that when he sees his image in you,


you show my tears beside his beauty, by which you grow rich: let his eyes at least behold them.
